---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import {atlas} from '../lib/catalogue';
import {formatNumber, github, path} from '../lib/format';
import {analyticsConfigured} from '../scripts/analytics';
const {stats} = atlas;
const files = [
  ['Places','places.json'],['Place aliases','place-aliases.json'],['Map points','places.geojson'],['Statistics','stats.json'],['Cities','cities.json'],
  ['Community reviews','reviews.json'],['Dated observations','observations.json'],['Curated trails','trails.json'],['Puff rankings','leaderboard.json'],
  ['Latest price and score by place','place-metrics.json'],['Mutta Puff Index','price-index.json'],
];
---
<Base title="About the atlas" description="Learn what Mutta Puffs Everywhere records, how the open atlas estimates coordinates, and how to download and reuse its data.">
  <div class="shell">
    <header class="page-head"><p class="kicker">About the project</p><h1>No puff left behind.</h1><p>Mutta Puffs Everywhere started as a shared map of places people remembered for egg puffs. It’s a place to record what you found and help someone else find it.</p></header>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>What’s in the atlas</h2>
      <p>Contributors have saved {formatNumber(stats.places)} places across {formatNumber(Object.keys(stats.countries).length)} countries. Browse {formatNumber(stats.cities)} city directories or use the Puff Map and district filters to find a spot. The Puff Guide brings together bakery trails, a random nearby pick, and a private visit diary.</p>
      <p><a href={path()}>Find puffs near you</a> · <a href={path('cities/')}>Browse cities</a> · <a href={path('guide/')}>Explore the Puff Guide</a></p>
      <h2>How the map works</h2>
      <p>The atlas preserves the latest crowdsourced export and its contributor notes. {formatNumber(stats.mappable)} places have coordinates, including {formatNumber(stats.accuracy.estimated ?? 0)} estimated from saved links. District names come from a dated boundary snapshot, and city areas include nearby towns. Each place page shows its source and coordinate accuracy.</p>
      <p>Choose device location to sort by straight-line distance. Your location stays in the tab. The basemap is hosted with the atlas, and opening an external map follows that provider’s privacy terms.</p>
      {import.meta.env.PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY && import.meta.env.PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_MAP_ID && <p>Choosing the Google basemap connects your browser to Google. <a href="https://www.google.com/intl/en_US/help/terms_maps/">Google Maps terms</a> · <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google privacy policy</a></p>}
      <h2 id="data">Open data</h2>
      <p>Version 1 exports are static files. GeoJSON includes entries with usable coordinates and marks their coordinate accuracy. The archive, reference boundaries, and independently submitted data have separate provenance.</p>
      <ul>{files.map(([label,file]) => <li><a href={path('api/v1/' + file)}>{label} · {file}</a></li>)}</ul>
      <p><a href={github + '/blob/main/data/mutta-puffs-everywhere.csv'}>Latest Maps export</a> · <a href={github + '/blob/main/DATA-LICENSE.md'}>Data sources and licensing</a> · <a href={path('schemas/v1/place.json')}>Place schema v1</a> · <a href={path('insights/')}>Atlas insights</a></p>
      <h2 id="privacy">Privacy</h2>
      <p>Passport entries and saved drafts use this browser’s storage. You control when to export or share them. If you enable Passport sync, the atlas encrypts your Passport in this browser before uploading the backup. Continuing on GitHub sends your contribution draft to GitHub for you to review and post.</p>
      {analyticsConfigured ? <>
        <p>Optional Umami analytics count page visits, chosen cities, directions clicks, searches with no matches, and handoffs to GitHub. The atlas sends page paths and selected public IDs, excluding coordinates, search text, private notes, and draft contents. The analytics host receives the usual connection information, including your IP address and browser.</p>
        <button class="button secondary" type="button" data-analytics-preference aria-pressed="false">Allow usage analytics</button>
        <p class="live-note" data-analytics-notice role="status"></p>
      </> : <p>Usage analytics are off. The atlas uses the published dataset for its public statistics.</p>}
      <h2>Help improve the atlas</h2>
      <p>Paste a shop link or use your location at the shop to start a draft. On supported Android browsers, the installed web app can also receive a shop or pin from the Maps share menu. Continue on GitHub when your contribution is ready for review.</p>
      <p>Help with a pin correction, photo, dated price, or the name of a stall behind a landmark.</p>
      <a class="button" href={path('contribute/')}>Contribute</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
